<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Agent's cross-section surface, carved into its own leaf project because two of its
    consumers are outside Shell:

      * AgentConversationRetentionJob (Humans.Infrastructure/Jobs) — recurring jobs are named
        by concrete type in Shell's UseHumansRecurringJobs roll-call and there is no
        ISection-style discovery seam for them yet (design §15.6b), so the job stays in Base
        and reaches the section through IAgentConversationRetention.
      * AnthropicBalanceProvider (Humans.Infrastructure/Services/Anthropic) does NOT appear
        here — it implements a Base-owned connector interface and the section consumes it.

    A Contracts/ *folder* inside Humans.Agent would therefore make Base reference a section
    and cycle (design §15.5b, memory/architecture/section-project-cycle-fix.md).

    IAgentAvailability and AgentSectionKeys are here for Shell rather than Base: Shell's
    HelpWidget/health checks need "is the agent on", and Shell's AgentPreloadAugmentor
    resolves the section keys the agent's own tool accepts. Both would have been fine in a
    folder; with the project forced into existence, everything cross-section lives in one
    place (the Events/Finance shape).

    References Humans.Interfaces only.
  -->

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Humans.Interfaces\Humans.Interfaces.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
